    Add support for extra data in adopter registration (#6802)
    
    This PR does a few things:
    - It adds support for arbitrary extra data to be sent as part of the
    normal adopter registration data. This enables (easier) extensions for
    things like tracking integrations like Tobira.
    - Adds a /stats endpoint for Tobira to put its stats information.
    - Cleans up the adopter registration code, renaming classes and removing
    redundant interfaces and such.
    
    Ideally this would go into a `r/17.x` release, however if it can't then
    `develop` would also work. This code adds a database table, but should
    not require changing existing schema.
    
    ### How to test this patch
    
    Start an instance of
    https://github.com/opencast/adopter-registration-server locally, setting
    `org.opencastproject.adopter.registration.server.url=http://localhost:5000/`
    in `custom.properties` prior to starting. Register as normal, restart
    Opencast (or the adopter registration bundle). Manual insert of data is
    required in the `/tobira/stats` endpoint, use the REST docs. The tobira
    parameters supported are `num_realms, num_blocks, version, config`.
    Omitted fields are silently ignored.
    
